   3. Known allergies to the study drug or any of its excipients; Or have experienced severe allergic reactions to other monoclonal antibodies;
4. Pregnant and lactating female patients, those with fertility and positive baseline pregnancy test results, or those of childbearing age who are unwilling to take effective contraceptive measures throughout the entire trial period.
